    "definition": "Six named, cited danger thresholds, split into two families. EXTERNAL/liquidity (the default triggers): Guidotti-Greenspan ST-debt>reserves; reserves<3mo imports; debt-service>25% exports. DOMESTIC/fiscal (a heavy but, in own currency, survivable load): debt>70% GDP; interest>20% revenue; interest>education. A stacked count of each family, not a weighted index — a country deep in domestic lines but none external (India, Japan) is heavy, not in danger.",
